摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Zero-dependency MCP client bridge for DeepSeek Harness: connect stdio/HTTP MCP servers and auto-register their tools for the agent.","id":"gh:1335759416","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-mcp-bridge","slug":"Chhlafiu4312/dsh-mcp-bridge","topics":["agent-tools","cordis","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","mcp","model-context-protocol"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Zero-dependency MCP client bridge for DeepSeek Harness: connect stdio/HTTP MCP servers and auto-regi"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"ster their tools for the agent."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-mcp-bridge"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**Connect the entire MCP ecosystem to DeepSeek Harness with one file. Zero dependencies. No SDK.**"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Your DSH agent gets every tool from any MCP server — filesystem, GitHub, databases, search, memory, "},{"id":"p4s2","text":"and thousands of community servers — as native tools it can call directly:"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## ✨ Why people use it"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"| 🔌 **One line to 1000+ tools** | The MCP ecosystem is the largest tool catalog for agents. This bri"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"dge plugs all of it into DSH. |\n| 🪶 **Zero dependencies** | Raw JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio, ~400 lines "},{"id":"p7s3","text":"of plain JavaScript. No SDK, no native modules. |\n| 🌐 **stdio + HTTP/SSE** | Local servers via `comm"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"and`, remote servers via `url` (bridged through `mcp-remote`). |\n| 🔁 **Auto-registration** | Every t"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"ool becomes `mcp_<server>_<tool>` the moment the server connects. |\n| 🧹 **Clean lifecycle** | Child "},{"id":"p7s6","text":"processes are terminated when the plugin stops or updates. |\n| 🛡️ **Honest boundaries** | Unsupporte"},{"id":"p7s7","text":"d JSON-Schema keywords degrade to open inputs — the MCP server stays the authority. |"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## 🚀 Quick start"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"**A. `dsh plugin add` (recommended — the repo is a `dsh.bundle`)**"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Then restart `dsh web` and configure servers via `DSH_MCP_SERVERS` (see below)."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"**B. Dynamic plugin (one session, no files)**"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Open a DSH session, ask your agent to run the bridge via `cordis_define` (paste the code from `plugi"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"n.js`), or define it yourself — then talk to it:"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"**C. Permanent (agent preset)**"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"The agent instantly sees tools like `mcp_filesystem_list_directory`, `mcp_github_create_issue`, … pl"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"us `mcp_status` to inspect every connection."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## 🔧 Configuration"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Servers are a JSON array. Each entry is either **stdio** or **url**:"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"| Field | Type | Meaning |"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"| `id` | string, required | tool prefix — tools become `mcp_<id>_<tool>` |\n| `command` + `args` | st"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"ring + string[] | stdio server executable and its argv |\n| `url` | string | remote server (HTTP/SSE,"},{"id":"p22s3","text":" bridged through `mcp-remote`) |\n| `cwd` | string | working directory (default: the process cwd) |\n|"},{"id":"p22s4","text":" `env` | object | extra environment variables |\n| `disabled` | boolean | listed in `mcp_status` but "},{"id":"p22s5","text":"never connected or validated |\n| `allowTools` / `denyTools` | string[] | exact-name filters, combina"},{"id":"p22s6","text":"ble — hide destructive tools |\n| `timeoutMs` | number | per-server call timeout in ms (default 12000"},{"id":"p22s7","text":"— hide destructive tools |\n| `timeoutMs` | number | per-server call timeout in ms (default 120000) |"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Set the array through `DSH_MCP_SERVERS` (JSON), or edit the defaults in `resolveServers()` inside `p"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"lugin.js`. Ready-made examples: `examples/servers.json` — filesystem, GitHub, fetch, memory, Postgre"},{"id":"p23s3","text":" Ready-made examples: `examples/servers.json` — filesystem, GitHub, fetch, memory, Postgres, remote."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"## 🧠 How it works"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Detailed walkthrough in docs/ARCHITECTURE.md:"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"1. **Spawn** — each configured server starts as a managed child process.\n2. **Handshake** — `initial"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"ize` + `notifications/initialized` over newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0.\n3. **Discover** — `tools/lis"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"t` returns every tool with its JSON Schema.\n4. **Register** — each tool is registered on the DSH too"},{"id":"p27s4","text":"ls registry; schemas are sanitized into the DSH parameter DSL.\n5. **Call** — the model calls the too"},{"id":"p27s5","text":"l; the bridge forwards `tools/call` and renders the text content back (120 s cooperative timeout, co"},{"id":"p27s6","text":"ncurrency-safe).\n6. **Teardown** — stopping the plugin unregisters the tools and terminates every pr"},{"id":"p27s7","text":"ncy-safe).\n6. **Teardown** — stopping the plugin unregisters the tools and terminates every process."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"## 🛣️ Roadmap"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"- [ ] Auto-reconnect with backoff\n- [ ] Native streamable-HTTP client (drop the `mcp-remote` depende"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"ncy for `url` servers)\n- [ ] Per-server permission prompts for destructive tools"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"## 🔒 Security notes"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"- MCP servers run with **your** permissions — only connect servers you trust.\n- The filesystem serve"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"r is scoped: give it only the directories the agent may touch.\n- API tokens travel through the `env`"},{"id":"p31s3","text":" field; prefer a secret manager or environment variables in production.\n- Full trust model and harde"},{"id":"p31s4","text":"ning advice: SECURITY.md."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"## ❓ FAQ"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"**Can I use my own MCP server?** Yes — anything that speaks MCP over stdio or streamable HTTP works."},{"id":"p33s2","text":" Point `command`/`args` at it (or `url` for remote servers) and its tools appear as `mcp_<id>_<tool>"},{"id":"p33s3","text":"oint `command`/`args` at it (or `url` for remote servers) and its tools appear as `mcp_<id>_<tool>`."},{"id":"p34s1","text":"**What happens when a server crashes?** The bridge retries up to 3 times with 2s/5s/10s backoff and "},{"id":"p34s2","text":"re-registers the tools on the new connection. Check `mcp_status` for the current state."},{"id":"p35s1","text":"**Do I need to restart DSH after changing config?** For the `dsh plugin`/preset install, yes — the c"},{"id":"p35s2","text":"onfig is read at plugin start. `disabled: true` keeps an entry configured without connecting it."},{"id":"p36s1","text":"**Why not the official MCP SDK?** The SDK would drag a dependency tree into a plugin that only needs"},{"id":"p36s2","text":" newline-delimited JSON-RPC. Zero dependencies keeps installs instant and reviewable (~400 lines)."},{"id":"p37s1","text":"**Does it support resources and prompts?** Yes — servers that declare those capabilities get `mcp_<s"},{"id":"p37s2","text":"erver>_list_resources`, `mcp_<server>_read_resource`, `mcp_<server>_list_prompts`, and `mcp_<server>"},{"id":"p37s3","text":"_get_prompt` tools automatically."},{"id":"p38s1","text":"**Upgrading from a pre-0.7.0 install?** The npm package was renamed to `dsh-mcp-connect` — remove th"},{"id":"p38s2","text":"e old dependency once so the two layers never both activate: `dsh plugin --profile web remove dsh-mc"},{"id":"p38s3","text":"ndency once so the two layers never both activate: `dsh plugin --profile web remove dsh-mcp-bridge`."},{"id":"p39s1","text":"**`npx`-based servers fail with `EPERM` / \"root-owned files\"?** Your npm cache was polluted by an ol"},{"id":"p39s2","text":"d `sudo npm` run. Either fix it once:"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"or sidestep it per server by giving `npx` a writable cache:"},{"id":"p42s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p43s1","text":"## 🛣️ 路线图 / 🔒 安全提示"},{"id":"p44s1","text":"路线图：resources/prompts 支持、断线自动重连、原生 streamable-HTTP 客户端、危险工具的逐服务器授权确认。安全：MCP server 以你的权限运行，只连接可信 ser"},{"id":"p44s2","text":"ver；filesystem server 只授予必要的目录；API token 走 `env` 字段，生产环境请用密钥管理器。"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
